      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Blocking also enables targeted harassment. It lets users single out a specific person and permanently exclude them from their experience. Friends can encourage each other to block the same person, leaving that person unable to participate in conversations with people who have decided they don't want to hear from them. The blocked user has no way to appeal that decision or require anyone to reconsider. Someone could block them once and never see their content again, even after they've changed. If that's a reason to reject content filters, it should apply to people too. Removing blocking would prevent this kind of exclusion and give every user a fair chance to keep explaining themselves until the other person agrees to interact with them.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
